  "findings": [
    "K is the lower path on five of six seeds and ties A on the sixth: A 281/382, K 228/382, A&K 186/382.",
    "The K-specific gap is larger than the A-specific gap: 95 rows have A but no K; 42 have K but no A; 59 have neither.",
    "K availability rises with cycle-36 U strength: pooled quartile rates are 31.8%, 49.5%, 80.8% and 89.1% from Q1 to Q4.",
    "The association is per-seed, but the high-U half still contains only 28\u201331 edges per seed, so U enrichment cannot by itself form a 60-row C1 stream.",
    "K scarcity is mostly absence, not lateness: 154/382 rows have no K in 120 cycles; only 28/228 available rows first form K after cycle 60.",
    "No tag is consistently absent across seeds. Pooled tag rates span 44.7\u201377.1%, but per-seed rates swing from 0.0 to 1.0; tag identity is not a stable redesign axis on these six seeds.",
    "K is almost entirely orientation-concordant: 278/286 candidate/reverse pairs agree (177 both, 101 neither); only 8 pairs differ. Reverse orientation is not a K lever.",
    "Local degree cannot explain the split: the candidate universe is near-regular (degree 8, or 7/8 on the 63-edge seeds)."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "K is measured in a no-arm replay over 120 cycles; it is not a treatment measurement.",
    "U is measured at cycle 36. The K\u2013U association has no identified direction: K may support later U, or both may share a cause.",
    "Tag rows count endpoint incidences, not edges; an edge contributes to two tags. Pooled tag rates are confounded with seed.",
    "Six seeds do not establish a world-family-wide structure.",
    "No target was selected, no threshold changed, no freeze or grant exists and no A1 cell ran."
  ],
  "redesign_arithmetic": "At 63\u201364 independent edges, reaching 60 K-available rows would require a K rate of 93.8\u201395.2%. The observed seeds are at 49.2\u201368.8%, and the high-U half is at 71.4\u201396.6% but has only 28\u201331 rows per seed. A larger independent universe lowers the required rate; 80 rows need 75%, 96 need 62.5%, and 120 need 50%. These are arithmetic requirements, not a proposed design.",
  "not_evidence": "A descriptive decomposition of existing no-arm artifacts. It does not identify a cause, select targets, set a threshold, choose a redesign or park A1."
